WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.888 --> 00:00:03.269
- [Narrator] On the surface,the
Ganesha Temple in Queens

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.397
seems like just a place
of worship for Hindus.

00:00:06.397 --> 00:00:07.264
- Hi.

00:00:07.264 --> 00:00:09.627
- [Narrator] But, if you
take the side entrance,

00:00:09.627 --> 00:00:11.205
down the hall with all the lights,

00:00:11.205 --> 00:00:13.336
follow the signs, down the stairs,

00:00:13.336 --> 00:00:16.235
follow more signs, down more stairs,

00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:18.818
you'll find the temple canteen.

00:00:20.235 --> 00:00:22.435
A restaurant serving
food to rival anything

00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:24.435
you would find in India.

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:31.565
This is Dr. Uma Mysorekar,

00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:32.475
- Namaste.

00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:34.484
I'm the President of
the Hindu Temple Society

00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:37.954
of North America in Flushing, New York.

00:00:37.954 --> 00:00:41.492
The temple came into existence in 1977.

00:00:41.492 --> 00:00:42.914
- [Narrator] And as one
of the first of its kind

00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:45.382
in North America, the temple
has become a cultural hub

00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:47.570
for Hindus throughout the US.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.604
- This is a place like home.

00:00:49.604 --> 00:00:52.652
People who come to the temple
spend their whole day here.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.394
They have their worshiping
services in the morning,

00:00:54.394 --> 00:00:56.892
and they very often
have cultural programs.

00:00:56.892 --> 00:00:59.172
But also, they come here to eat.

00:00:59.172 --> 00:01:00.673
- [Narrator] They come
to the temple to eat?

00:01:00.673 --> 00:01:02.474
- Yes, they do come here to eat.

00:01:02.474 --> 00:01:04.092
Some of them come just only to eat,

00:01:04.092 --> 00:01:07.274
not even to come inside the temple.

00:01:07.274 --> 00:01:09.162
- [Narrator] So, in addition
to a place of worship,

00:01:09.162 --> 00:01:11.522
a community center and a wedding venue,

00:01:11.522 --> 00:01:15.061
the Ganesha Temple serves
cuisine authentic to South India

00:01:15.061 --> 00:01:16.631
and is open to the public.

00:01:16.631 --> 00:01:19.042
And the food is pretty fantastic.

00:01:19.042 --> 00:01:21.620
Just ask the New York
Times, or New York Magazine,

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:22.941
or Anthony Bourdain.

00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:24.229
- [Anthony] This is delicious.

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:27.471
- [Uma] It's not easy to find
our Indian food everywhere

00:01:27.471 --> 00:01:29.101
around the corners, so people come

00:01:29.101 --> 00:01:31.712
to find authentic Indian food.

00:01:31.712 --> 00:01:33.750
- [Narrator] Okay, so if
you don't know anything

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:37.472
about South Indian food, here
are some of the must-haves.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:38.704
There's vada.

00:01:38.704 --> 00:01:41.363
- [Uma] I always called it salty donuts.

00:01:41.363 --> 00:01:42.196
- [Narrator] Idli.

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:43.373
- [Uma] It is nothing but puffed rice.

00:01:43.373 --> 00:01:44.904
- [Narrator] Sambar.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.012
- [Uma] It is made of lentils.

00:01:46.012 --> 00:01:47.032
Very healthy.

00:01:47.032 --> 00:01:48.533
- [Narrator] And most notably, dosas.

00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:50.213
- [Uma] There are at
least about eight or nine

00:01:50.213 --> 00:01:51.883
kinds of dosas.

00:01:51.883 --> 00:01:55.104
It consists of dough, and
there is a filling inside.

00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:57.687
We have authentic Indian cooks.

00:02:00.736 --> 00:02:02.920
In our Hinduism we strongly believe,

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.877
without the offering
of food to the deities

00:02:05.877 --> 00:02:10.440
our prayer is incomplete, and
that's how it really started.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.661
But I think when you go to
a canteen or a restaurant,

00:02:13.661 --> 00:02:15.739
you want to enjoy your food.

00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:18.987
We want to make sure that
whether it is a Hindu

00:02:18.987 --> 00:02:23.070
or a non-Hindu, should be
able to enjoy the food.

00:02:24.485 --> 00:02:25.877
Who cares really whether it is

00:02:25.877 --> 00:02:28.226
an Indian restaurant or
a non-Indian restaurant,

00:02:28.226 --> 00:02:30.485
you just want to go and eat food.

00:02:30.485 --> 00:02:32.517
- [Narrator] So the next
time you're hungry in Queens,

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:33.767
try the temple.

